{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>They did well in all that they spoke.</b> Meaning, that they accepted upon themselves to do the words of the prophet and to justify him, and concerning this he concluded: ״מִי יִתֵּן וְהָיָה״ etc. And they of blessed memory said (Avodah Zarah 5a) that Moses erred in that he did not say to them ״תֵּן אַתָּה״ — for had he said thus, they would not have harbored suspicions against Moses, neither regarding the sending of spies nor regarding the dispute of Korah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:15:27.289464414Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}